# Milestone: v0.13.3 (design-risks v0.13.1-B)
# Covers: a finally body's replacement unwind absorbed at an OUTER handler
#         (catch in the caller) lets the strand continue as NORMAL code —
#         a subsequent park (sleep in the catch handler) is legitimate
#         control flow, not a mid-cleanup truncation.
#         Pre-fix: run_cleanup_with_replace misread the post-absorption
#         park as a truncated cleanup body and escalated to a spurious
#         CLEANUP_OVERFLOW fatal — the strand died, the sleep never
#         resumed, and Realm.r stayed 0.
#         Post-fix (s->cleanup_absorbed): the strand parks normally and
#         resumes after the clock advances; Realm.r == 9 (the finally's
#         throw replaced the suppressed `return 5` per C-1).
## timeout: 30
## host: run Realm.r = 0
## host: run var g = function() { try { return 5 } finally { throw(9) } }
## host: run try { Realm.x = Realm.g() } catch (var e) { sleep(10ms); Realm.r = e }
## host: run Realm.r
## host: advance-clock 20
## host: step 100000
## host: run Realm.r
[00000000] 0
[00000000] <?>
[00000000] nil
[00000000] 0
[00000000] step: QUIESCENT
[00000000] 9
